 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Weather is the state of the air on one day (rain, sun, wind). Climate is the usual pattern of weather in a place over many years (for example, a long dry season in the north, heavy rains in Debundscha).\nClimate change is a lasting change in these patterns, caused today mainly by global warming: rains come late or stop early, rainy seasons are shorter but more violent, dry seasons hotter.\nEffects on daily life: farmers do not know when to plant, harvests fall, food prices rise, water is scarce, floods and landslides destroy homes.\nAdaptation (living with it): drought-resistant crops, storing rain water, irrigation, building away from flood zones, early warnings. Mitigation (reducing it): cutting greenhouse gases.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Is one very hot day climate change?",
  "steps": [
   "One hot day is weather.",
   "Climate change is a lasting change in the pattern of weather over many years."
  ],
  "answer": "No: one day is weather; climate change is long-term.",
  "checks": []
 },
